## 🚀 Overview

NexusChat is designed to demonstrate real-time communication using WebSocket-based events. It connects browser clients to a Node.js server and updates conversations and online-user information as events happen.

## ✨ Features

- 💬 **Public Messaging** — Send messages in a shared chat.
- 🔒 **Private Messaging** — Exchange private messages.
- 🟢 **Online User Updates** — See user presence updates.
- 🔔 **Join & Leave Notifications** — Get notified when users enter or leave.
- ⚡ **Real-Time Communication** — Powered by Socket.IO.
- 🎨 **Interactive Interface** — Built with EJS, JavaScript and CSS.

## 🛠️ Technology Stack

| Technology | Role |
|---|---|
| Node.js | JavaScript runtime |
| Express.js | Backend web framework |
| Socket.IO | Real-time event communication |
| EJS | Server-rendered templates |
| JavaScript | Application functionality |
| HTML5 & CSS3 | User interface |

## ⚙️ Run Locally

### Prerequisites

- Node.js
- npm
- Git

### Installation

**1. Clone the repository**

```bash
git clone https://github.com/theharshadramayane-ship-IT/NexusChat.git
```

**2. Navigate to the project**

```bash
cd NexusChat
```

**3. Install dependencies**

```bash
npm install
```

**4. Start the server**

```bash
npm start
```

**5. Open the application**

Visit `http://localhost:3000` in your browser.

